1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,090
In this lesson, you'll learn three
time-savers: snippets for the questions you

2
00:00:05,090 --> 00:00:08,327
answer every day, templates
for emails, and scheduling,

3
00:00:08,327 --> 00:00:12,152
so your messages go out at the
right time, even when you're busy.

4
00:00:13,069 --> 00:00:17,715
You probably answer the same questions
every week: prices, opening hours,

5
00:00:17,715 --> 00:00:18,479
how to book.

6
00:00:18,479 --> 00:00:22,743
Snippets are saved replies your
whole team can insert in one click.

7
00:00:22,743 --> 00:00:26,943
You'll find them in the Snippets
tab, at the top of Conversations.

8
00:00:27,792 --> 00:00:29,489
Notice the curly brackets.

9
00:00:29,489 --> 00:00:31,055
Those are custom values.

10
00:00:31,055 --> 00:00:36,405
When you insert a snippet, {{contact.first_name}}
is swapped for the person's real

11
00:00:36,405 --> 00:00:39,537
first name, so every reply
still feels personal.

12
00:00:40,393 --> 00:00:41,359
Let's add one.

13
00:00:41,359 --> 00:00:45,635
Click Add Snippet and give it a
name your team will recognise.

14
00:00:45,635 --> 00:00:49,015
Choose Text for SMS,
WhatsApp and chat, or Email.

15
00:00:49,015 --> 00:00:50,601
Then write the message.

16
00:00:50,601 --> 00:00:54,257
The Custom values button
adds the first name for you.

17
00:00:55,807 --> 00:00:58,767
Pick a folder to keep
things tidy, then save.

18
00:00:58,767 --> 00:01:02,976
Good names matter: start with the
topic, like parking or prices,

19
00:01:02,976 --> 00:01:04,686
so they're easy to search.

20
00:01:04,686 --> 00:01:09,750
The snippet is now available to everyone
on your team, in every conversation.

21
00:01:10,601 --> 00:01:11,761
Now let's use one.

22
00:01:11,761 --> 00:01:16,013
Open a conversation and click the
snippets button in the composer.

23
00:01:16,013 --> 00:01:18,976
Search, or scroll, and
click the one you need.

24
00:01:18,976 --> 00:01:23,293
It drops into the message box with
Olivia's name already filled in.

25
00:01:23,293 --> 00:01:25,290
Check it reads well, then send.

26
00:01:27,253 --> 00:01:29,465
For emails, you also get templates.

27
00:01:29,465 --> 00:01:31,615
Daniel wants to move his check-up.

28
00:01:31,615 --> 00:01:36,482
His conversation is on email, so open
Templates and pick "Appointment moved".

29
00:01:36,482 --> 00:01:39,263
The subject and the
message fill in for you.

30
00:01:40,116 --> 00:01:43,655
Say you only get to Daniel's
email late in the evening.

31
00:01:43,655 --> 00:01:45,586
A reply at midnight looks odd.

32
00:01:45,586 --> 00:01:49,576
Instead of Send, click the clock
icon to schedule the message.

33
00:01:49,576 --> 00:01:52,601
Pick the date and the
time, and click Schedule.

34
00:01:53,451 --> 00:01:58,282
The message now waits in the thread, with
a dashed outline and the time it will go

35
00:01:58,282 --> 00:01:58,518
out.

36
00:01:58,518 --> 00:01:59,578
Changed your mind?

37
00:01:59,578 --> 00:02:02,877
Click Cancel any time before
then, and it won't be sent.

38
00:02:03,731 --> 00:02:06,796
Scheduling is perfect for
follow-ups you've promised.

39
00:02:06,796 --> 00:02:09,456
Write the message while
the details are fresh,

40
00:02:09,456 --> 00:02:12,463
schedule it for the morning
you agreed, and move on.

41
00:02:12,463 --> 00:02:17,205
Kyntlo sends it on time, from your business
number, even if you're with a patient.

42
00:02:18,056 --> 00:02:20,232
The composer has a few more helpers.

43
00:02:20,232 --> 00:02:24,945
Add an emoji, attach a file like an
aftercare guide, or insert a trigger link,

44
00:02:24,945 --> 00:02:26,577
which tracks who clicks it.

45
00:02:26,577 --> 00:02:29,538
You'll find those links
in the Trigger Links tab.

46
00:02:30,387 --> 00:02:31,494
Here's a pro tip.

47
00:02:31,494 --> 00:02:34,554
Build your snippet library
from real questions.

48
00:02:34,554 --> 00:02:39,632
For one week, every time you type the
same answer twice, save it as a snippet.

49
00:02:39,632 --> 00:02:43,344
By Friday, most of your replies
will take a single click.

50
00:02:44,195 --> 00:02:46,673
That's snippets, templates and scheduling!

51
00:02:46,673 --> 00:02:49,446
Next, you'll put a chat
widget on your website,

52
00:02:49,446 --> 00:02:52,573
so visitors can message you
straight into this inbox.

53
00:02:52,573 --> 00:02:53,399
See you there.
